  "note": "calculateMRC takes the MAX grade among fired mrc-rules.js rules (MRC 1 default when none fire). detectAdditionalFlags is fully independent. Verified engine quirk: PF-004 ('Reduced FEV1/FVC ratio') compares fev1FvcRatio < 70, not < 0.7, even though the ratio is stored as a 0-1 fraction elsewhere in this same form (pulmonaryFunction.fev1FvcRatio) - so PF-004 fires whenever the field is answered with any realistic fraction (e.g. 0.68), regardless of whether the patient's airflow is actually obstructed. This is a genuine, verified divergence from the sibling forms' spirometry rules (e.g. pulmonology-assessment's own GOLD rules correctly compare the same kind of ratio against 0.7), left as-is per the mirrored-engine convention rather than silently patched here. The baseline persona below leaves fev1FvcRatio unanswered specifically to avoid this quirk firing in a case meant to have zero fired rules.",
